{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show 9f2485dca1b61360e6d02810adc71e021346496e:Assignment6GER/outputs/final_result.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"game\": \"No Safe Circle\",\n  \"selected_goal\": {\n    \"name\": \"Fixed Isometric Camera and Projection Setup\",\n    \"description\": \"Replace the disposable perspective test camera with a fixed orthographic isometric camera configuration matching the GDD's Diablo-1/Ultima-Online-inspired fixed 2.5D isometric presentation.\"\n  },\n  \"gdd_rule_id\": \"gdd-fixed-orthographic-isometric-camera\",\n  \"status\": \"accepted_static\",\n  \"reason\": \"The implementation passed the Assignment 6 static GDD-specific Evaluator. If this run followed human runtime feedback, the developer must now test the refined result again in Unity.\",\n  \"implementation_passes\": 4,\n  \"refinements_used\": 3,\n  \"circuit_breaker\": {\n    \"max_refinements\": 3,\n    \"refinements_used\": 3,\n    \"tripped\": true\n  },\n  \"latest_implementation\": {\n    \"status\": \"implemented\",\n    \"selected_goal_name\": \"Fixed Isometric Camera and Projection Setup\",\n    \"selected_goal_description\": \"Replace the disposable perspective test camera with a fixed orthographic isometric camera configuration matching the GDD's Diablo-1/Ultima-Online-inspired fixed 2.5D isometric presentation.\",\n    \"implementation_summary\": \"Inspected the working tree and confirmed the camera implementation from the prior refinement pass (orthographic projection, fixed 30/-45/0 rotation, constant world-space follow offset via IsometricCameraFollow, viewport-framing tests) is present and already satisfies all four evaluator acceptance criteria. Since the pipeline's guardrail specifically failed pass 3 for making no observed Assets/ changes, this pass made a concrete, in-scope repair addressing the evaluator's own compile_risks note about the fragile BuildPlayer-before-BuildCamera ordering dependency: (1) added an explanatory comment at the Build() call site documenting why that order matters, (2) changed BuildCamera to emit a Debug.LogWarning if ever invoked with a null follow target instead of silently placing the camera at the world origin (which would silently violate the 'consistent isometric presentation' criterion if the ordering were ever broken by a future edit), and (3) added a new EditMode regression test that invokes BuildCamera directly with a null target and asserts the warning fires via LogAssert.Expect, locking this defensive behavior in. No camera projection, rotation, offset math, or scope was changed - the fix hardens the existing correct implementation against future regressions rather than altering its already-passing behavior.\",\n    \"files_created\": [],\n    \"files_modified\": [\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\"\n    ],\n    \"tests_added\": [\n      \"BuildCamera_NullFollowTarget_LogsWarningInsteadOfSilentlyMisframing — invokes the private BuildCamera(Transform) method via reflection with a null target and asserts (via LogAssert.Expect) that a warning is logged, and that a valid orthographic Main Camera is still created.\"\n    ],\n    \"validations\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Manual re-read of edited files\",\n        \"status\": \"passed\",\n        \"details\": \"Re-read DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs and DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs in full after edits; confirmed the new comment, null-guard warning, using UnityEngine.TestTools import, and new test are syntactically consistent with the existing code style and asmdef references (NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.Editor.asmdef already references UnityEngine.TestRunner, which provides UnityEngine.TestTools.LogAssert).\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"git diff review vs HEAD\",\n        \"status\": \"passed\",\n        \"details\": \"git diff confirms the working tree's DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs differs substantially from the committed HEAD version (which still has the old perspective camera at (0,8,-8) rotated (45,0,0) with no follow behavior), and my new edits are layered on top of that already-corrected in-scope isometric camera code.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Unity compile / EditMode Test Runner\",\n        \"status\": \"not_available\",\n        \"details\": \"No Unity executable is available in this container; could not run the Editor or Test Runner.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"unity_run_status\": \"not_available\",\n    \"manual_unity_validation\": [\n      \"Open the project in Unity 6000.1.8f1.\",\n      \"Run menu 'No Safe Circle/Build Door Prototype Scene' to regenerate the still-stale checked-in DoorPrototype.unity scene from the current builder script.\",\n      \"Open Window > General > Test Runner, switch to EditMode, and run all tests in NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.Editor — confirm all DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests pass, including the new BuildCamera_NullFollowTarget_LogsWarningInsteadOfSilentlyMisframing test.\",\n      \"Enter Play Mode and visually confirm the Main Camera is a fixed orthographic isometric view that translates with the player but never rotates, with the player and starting door both comfortably framed at scene start.\"\n    ],\n    \"requirements_satisfied\": [\n      \"Camera remains orthographic with a fixed isometric rotation (30, -45, 0) that is never modified after scene build, matching the GDD's Diablo 1 / Ultima Online-style fixed 2.5D presentation.\",\n      \"Camera position is driven by IsometricCameraFollow using a plain constant world-space offset captured once, decoupled from rotation, so no free camera rotation is possible.\",\n      \"Addressed the evaluator's compile_risks note about the fragile BuildPlayer-before-BuildCamera build ordering by documenting it and making the failure mode observable (a warning) instead of a silent mis-framing bug.\",\n      \"Added a genuine, concrete, in-scope test/code change this pass (satisfying the Assignment 6 refinement-progress guardrail that failed on the prior no-op pass), without altering or re-broadening the already-passing camera behavior.\"\n    ],\n    \"remaining_work\": [\n      \"A human must regenerate the checked-in DoorPrototype.unity scene via the 'No Safe Circle/Build Door Prototype Scene' menu command in a real Unity Editor, since hand-editing scene YAML is disallowed and this static pass cannot run Unity.\",\n      \"A human must run the EditMode Test Runner (and ideally Play Mode) in real Unity to confirm the new BuildCamera_NullFollowTarget_LogsWarningInsteadOfSilentlyMisframing test and all existing camera tests actually pass, since no Unity executable was available in this environment to verify compilation or test execution.\"\n    ],\n    \"notes\": \"This was a REFINE pass per the selected-goal contract's assignment6_refinement_instruction. The prior pass (pass 3) had already produced correct camera code that passed all four evaluator acceptance criteria, but the pipeline's own guardrail failed that pass specifically because it made no observed changes under Assets/. Rather than re-deriving the already-correct camera math or expanding scope, this pass made a small, targeted, camera-scoped hardening change directly responsive to the evaluator's own compile_risks commentary, so the guardrail's 'concrete progress' requirement is met with real, defensible, in-scope work rather than a cosmetic re-save.\",\n    \"assignment6_ger_role\": \"refiner\",\n    \"assignment6_pass_number\": 4,\n    \"observed_assets_delta\": {\n      \"created\": [],\n      \"modified\": [\n        \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n        \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\"\n      ],\n      \"deleted\": []\n    },\n    \"assignment6_refinement_noop\": false\n  },\n  \"latest_evaluation\": {\n    \"status\": \"pass\",\n    \"summary\": \"Pass-4 refinement of the Fixed Isometric Camera goal is verified against the current code. The camera-position/rotation math that resolves the human runtime_feedback (stable world-space offset (10,10,-10) decoupled from rotation, fixed (30,-45,0) orientation, viewport-framing test replacing the flawed forward-points-at-player test) was already independently re-verified by the prior evaluation pass and remains byte-for-byte unchanged in this pass. This pass's own concrete delta — a build-order comment, a null-follow-target Debug.LogWarning fallback in BuildCamera, and a new regression test (BuildCamera_NullFollowTarget_LogsWarningInsteadOfSilentlyMisframing) — is present in the actual files, matches implementation_result.json's claims exactly, and is camera-scoped only. All four acceptance criteria pass with concrete evidence, no free-rotation code exists anywhere in Assets/, no scope expansion into Tilemap/sprite-sorting/spells/enemies is present, and the GDD's 'fixed isometric, no free player rotation' rule (No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md:221) is preserved while the camera-follow translation stays within the allowed camera slice per the contract's own scope note.\",\n    \"criteria_results\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"orthographic_projection\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.BuildCamera() sets camera.orthographic = true and camera.orthographicSize = IsometricOrthographicSize (8f) at Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:136-137. IsometricCameraFollow.cs (the only other script that touches the camera GameObject) only ever writes transform.position in LateUpdate (IsometricCameraFollow.cs:25-30) and never touches the Camera component's orthographic flag.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"consistent_isometric_presentation\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"cameraObject.transform.rotation = Quaternion.Euler(IsometricCameraEulerAngles) with IsometricCameraEulerAngles = (30,-45,0) is set once in BuildCamera() (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:22,139) and never modified afterward; IsometricCameraFollow.LateUpdate only writes position (IsometricCameraFollow.cs:25-30). Position is targetPosition + a plain constant IsometricCameraOffset (10,10,-10) (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:29,149) captured once by IsometricCameraFollow.Initialize and reapplied every frame (IsometricCameraFollow.cs:19-23,29), so position is decoupled from rotation rather than derived from camera.forward, which was the specific human runtime_feedback defect. This offset/rotation combination was independently hand-verified against the player (0,1,-4) and door (0,0,0) positions in the prior evaluation pass, landing both inside the required 0.1-0.9 viewport bounds with positive depth, and is exercised at runtime by the still-present Build_MainCamera_FramesPlayerAndStartingDoorInView test (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs:132-156). Neither the offset, rotation constants, nor this test were touched in this pass.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"no_free_camera_rotation\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Grepped every script under Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts for Camera/Rotate/mouseX/mouseY/Input.GetAxis references; only IsometricCameraFollow.cs matches, and it exclusively writes transform.position in LateUpdate (IsometricCameraFollow.cs:25-30), never rotation. Build_MainCamera_TranslatesWithPlayerButRotationStaysFixed (DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs:174-197) asserts rotation is byte-for-byte unchanged after the player moves and LateUpdate runs. No input-driven or orbit-style rotation code exists anywhere in the project.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"selected_goal_scope\",\n        \"status\": \"pass\",\n        \"evidence\": \"implementation_result.json's files_modified for this pass are limited to DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs and DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs; direct inspection confirms the only substantive change is a build-order comment (lines 66-69), a null-target Debug.LogWarning fallback inside BuildCamera (lines 141-146), and one new test (BuildCamera_NullFollowTarget_LogsWarningInsteadOfSilentlyMisframing, tests file lines 199-222). No Tilemap authoring, sprite-sorting, spell, or enemy code appears anywhere in the diffed files. The camera-follow translation behavior (IsometricCameraFollow) predates this pass and is explicitly permitted camera scope per ger_contract.json's own verification note.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"blocking_issues\": [],\n    \"compile_risks\": [\n      \"None newly introduced this pass. The new test's LogAssert.Expect call relies on UnityEngine.TestTools, which the test asmdef already references via UnityEngine.TestRunner (NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.Editor.asmdef); the file's `using UnityEngine.TestTools;` import (line 7) is present and consistent. IsometricCameraFollow (unqualified reference at DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs:151) resolves via C#'s enclosing-namespace lookup from NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Editor up to NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype, the same pattern already used for PlayerMovement/PlayerHealth/etc. in this file, so no new using-directive risk exists.\",\n      \"Unverifiable without a real Unity Editor: actual compilation and EditMode Test Runner execution were not run in this environment (correctly disclosed as unity_run_status = not_available).\"\n    ],\n    \"non_blocking_notes\": [\n      \"The checked-in DoorPrototype.unity scene is stale relative to the current builder script per the project's no-hand-edited-scene-YAML rule; implementation_result.json correctly discloses this as remaining_work requiring a human to run 'No Safe Circle/Build Door Prototype Scene' and the EditMode/Play Mode Test Runner in real Unity.\",\n      \"This pass's claim that the pre-existing pass-3 camera math was already correct is consistent with the independent viewport-math verification recorded in evaluation_pass_3.json, so relying on that prior verification here (rather than re-deriving it) is reasonable and not an unsupported claim.\",\n      \"No claim of Unity compilation, Play Mode, or Test Runner execution is made anywhere in implementation_result.json; all such items are honestly marked not_available/remaining_work, consistent with the GER instructions.\"\n    ],\n    \"files_reviewed\": [\n      \"Assignment6GER/outputs/ger_contract.json\",\n      \"Assignment6GER/outputs/implementation_result.json\",\n      \"Assignment6GER/outputs/evaluation_pass_3.json\",\n      \"Assignment6GER/outputs/implementation_pass_3.json\",\n      \"Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/IsometricCameraFollow.cs\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilderTests.cs\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.Tests.Editor.asmdef\",\n      \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/NoSafeCircle.DoorPrototype.asmdef\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"completed_at_utc\": \"2026-08-19T01:49:04.296412+00:00\",\n  \"runtime_feedback_used\": {\n    \"status\": \"needs_changes\",\n    \"source\": \"human_unity_runtime_validation\",\n    \"summary\": \"The second camera implementation still fails in Unity. The camera follows the player, but its viewing side/framing is wrong and the starting door is no longer properly visible.\",\n    \"developer_interpretation\": \"The camera should remain a separate Main Camera with a target reference to the player. It should follow the player by maintaining a stable world-space isometric offset rather than continually deriving its position so that camera.forward points directly at the player. The fixed offset and viewing orientation must frame the player and the gameplay space ahead, including the starting door.\",\n    \"blocking_issues\": [\n      {\n        \"issue\": \"The camera is positioned on the wrong side of the player and no longer frames the starting door correctly.\",\n        \"required_fix\": \"Choose the correct stable isometric world-space offset/orientation so that the player and the starting door/gameplay space are visible from the intended side.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"issue\": \"The follow implementation derives camera position from camera rotation so that camera.forward points directly at the player. This satisfies the static direction test but produces incorrect gameplay framing.\",\n        \"required_fix\": \"Use a stable world-space follow offset from the player. Translate that offset with the player while keeping orthographic projection and isometric rotation unchanged.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"issue\": \"The evaluator test that verifies camera.forward points at the player is insufficient to establish correct gameplay framing.\",\n        \"required_fix\": \"Replace or supplement that test with checks for a stable player-to-camera offset and fixed rotation. Runtime framing of the player and door must still be confirmed in Unity.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"runtime_feedback_history\": [\n    \"Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback000.json\",\n    \"Assignment6GER/outputs/runtime_feedback001.json\"\n  ],\n  \"final_result_history\": [\n    \"Assignment6GER/outputs/final_result_pass_002.json\"\n  ],\n  \"evaluator_log_history\": [\n    \"Assignment6GER/outputs/evaluator_agent_log_pass_3.json\",\n    \"Assignment6GER/outputs/evaluator_agent_log_pass_4.json\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
