\"AC-002\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"GDD §2 Health feedback\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Provides a continuous player-facing health indicator reflecting current/maximum health at all times.\",\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-003\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"GDD §2 Loss / Floor-run restart ownership\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Exposes an owner-controlled reset entry point restoring current health to its floor-initial value, consumed by the Floor Run/Restart Orchestrator.\",\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-004\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"GDD §2 Resources, Feedback, and Failure\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Health does not passively regenerate during or between rooms; it changes only through the owner-controlled damage interface, the owner-controlled restore interface (door-lock recovery), or the orchestrator-invoked floor reset.\",\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-005\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"completion_gates\": [\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"GDD §3 Player Experience Success Criteria\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Validate that failure is readable through health/damage feedback (contributing cause alongside positioning, mana, and timing failures).\",\n      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-001\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"Section 3 - Player Experience Success Criteria\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Failure caused by poor positioning is readable to the player through health/damage feedback, as part of the required 'failure is readable' success criterion.\",\n      \"gate_id\": \"VAL-002\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"downstream_integration_obligations\": [],\n  \"gdd_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"GDD §2 Resources, Feedback, and Failure — Player Health ownership\",\n      \"requirement\": \"The shared Player Health system is the single owner of current health, exposing owner-controlled damage and restore interfaces plus an observable zero-health/death transition consumed by the Floor Run/Restart Orchestrator; restoration is clamped to maximum health and other systems never write player-health state directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"GDD §2 Resources, Feedback, and Failure — Health feedback\",\n      \"requirement\": \"The wizard's current health is continuously visible through a simple player-facing health indicator so accumulated damage is readable across the whole run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reference\": \"GDD §2 Loss / Floor-run restart ownership\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Player Health is a required reset participant with an owner-controlled reset entry point invoked by the Floor Run/Restart Orchestrator.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"basis\": \"direct_gdd\",\n  \"source_scope\": \"required\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"notes\": \"Exact fixed door-lock recovery amount is an explicitly deferred playtesting value per GDD; this item only needs to expose the clamped restore interface, not decide the tuning number.\",\n  \"repository_state_at_bootstrap\": \"partial\",\n  \"repository_evidence_at_bootstrap\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerHealth.cs\",\n      \"evidence_type\": \"code\",\n      \"observation\": \"Implements CurrentHealth, a clamped TakeDamage(amount) damage interface, and a Damaged event; has no restore/heal method, no zero-health/death event, and no reset entry point.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\",\n      \"evidence_type\": \"scene\",\n      \"observation\": \"PlayerHealth.cs (guid ddabb8b125ed06f42863f611de5826f7) is serialized on the Player GameObject, confirming the current damage-only implementation is integrated.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scripts/PlayerInteractionController.cs\",\n      \"evidence_type\": \"code\",\n      \"observation\": \"Subscribes to PlayerHealth.Damaged to cancel an in-progress door interaction, confirming the existing damage event is consumed elsewhere, but no analogous health-UI or death-event consumer exists.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"origin\": \"verified_reconciliation_bootstrap\",\n    \"source_schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"reconciliation_run_id\": \"20260821T193541Z-998ee7b5\",\n    \"verification_run_id\": \"20260821T195959Z-43dba5de\",\n    \"bootstrap_status_observation\": \"open\",\n    \"migration_id\": \"task-contract-schema-v2-20260822-r2\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
