{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"alternative_architecture\":{\"description\":\"\",\"needed\":true,\"why_better\":\"\"},\"architecture_summary\":\"A concrete moving-canon failure is now verified. Commit 484e66a moved the sole authoritative scene to Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity, but the frozen GDD still declares the deleted nested path canonical and calls Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity a non-canonical stub. The production RAG correctly hashes and indexes that semantically stale GDD; numerous live task contracts and resource locks still point at the deleted scene, and NSC-037 explicitly forbids registering the scene that is now authoritative. Freshness-by-hash therefore proves byte synchronization, not truth, and the current task/resource graph can misdirect work or fail to lock the actual shared Unity asset.\",\"biggest_uncertainty\":\"\",\"confidence\":0,\"do_not_build_yet\":[],\"evidence\":[{\"observation\":\"The authoritative scene was moved without updating GDD or task/resource contracts.\",\"path\":\"Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity\"},{\"observation\":\"Canon still names the deleted scene path and misclassifies the actual canonical scene.\",\"path\":\"Docs/GDD/No_Safe_Circle_GDD.md\"},{\"observation\":\"A live build task prohibits the now-authoritative scene and requires the deleted one.\",\"path\":\"Tasks/NSC-037.yaml\"},{\"observation\":\"The production index can be byte-current while faithfully retrieving stale repository-state claims.\",\"path\":\"Pipeline/GDDRAG/knowledge_base/No_Safe_Circle_GDD_RAG.json\"}],\"gdd_iteration_concerns\":[\"Whole-document hash freshness detects edits but cannot determine whether canon remains semantically synchronized with implementation facts.\",\"Task references are free-text section labels rather than stable requirement identities, so scoped impact and traceable requirement revision are absent.\"],\"human_intervention_points\":[],\"hypothetical_failure_solutions\":[],\"missing_components\":[],\"next_slice\":{\"deliverables\":[],\"proof_of_value\":\"\",\"title\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"},\"observed_failure_solutions\":[],\"overall_verdict\":\"partially_unsound\",\"overengineering\":[],\"state_and_authority_concerns\":[\"Resource authority drifted: task locks name a deleted scene, while the real shared scene is unlocked by those contracts.\"],\"strong_decisions\":[],\"structural_flaws\":[\"The architecture conflates design canon with time-stamped repository evidence and pipeline policy inside one GDD.\",\"Hash freshness is treated as a sufficient integrity boundary even when the source itself is semantically stale.\"],\"throughput_assessment\":\"\",\"verdict_reason\":\"\"}"}}
