t dispatch is mandatory; unrelated repository context is withheld unless the active task requires it.\"\n--\n100-      ],\n101-      \"evidence\": \"Directly stated as required process/handoff structure in Section 4 and reiterated in Section 5 Agent Coordination.\"\n102-    },\n103-    {\n104:      \"title\": \"Human inspection and final integration authority\",\n105-      \"requirement_type\": \"pipeline_constraint\",\n106-      \"status\": \"confirmed\",\n107-      \"gdd_evidence\": [\n108-        {\n109-          \"reference\": \"Section 5 - API and Tool Constraints\",\n110:          \"requirement\": \"Unity scenes, prefab references, animations, and Inspector assignments require human inspection. Agent-generated work is not merged until its Play Mode checklist has been tested.\"\n111-        },\n112-        {\n113-          \"reference\": \"Section 4 - Shared Context and Coordination Rules\",\n114:          \"requirement\": \"The human developer remains responsible for architecture, merging changes, inspecting Unity scenes and prefabs, playtesting, balance, and final integration.\"\n115-        }\n116-      ],\n117:      \"evidence\": \"Explicitly stated as required human-authority process constraints in Sections 4 and 5.\"\n118-    },\n119-    {\n120-      \"title\": \"Agent scope and canon discipline\",\n121-      \"requirement_type\": \"pipeline_constraint\",\n--\n160-      ],\n161-      \"evidence\": \"Directly stated in Section 5 Runtime Implementation and reiterated in the Technical Strategy generative-tools note; a required process/validation constraint on content/asset pipeline work rather than gameplay implementation.\"\n162-    },\n163-    {\n164:      \"title\": \"Non-canonical prototype scene preservation\",\n165-      \"requirement_type\": \"pipeline_constraint\",\n166-      \"status\": \"confirmed\",\n167-      \"gdd_evidence\": [\n168-        {\n169-          \"reference\": \"Section 5 - Current Prototype Scene Evidence\",\n170:          \"requirement\": \"The presence of the non-canonical Assets/Scenes stub scenes is repository evidence, not a design requirement; their deletion, retention, or repurposing is a human decision, and agents/reconciliation steps must not delete or reinterpret them merely to make scene inventory evidence cleaner.\"\n171-        }\n172-      ],\n173:      \"evidence\": \"Directly stated in Section 5 Current Prototype Scene Evidence; confirmed present via Assets/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity and Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity glob results.\"\n174-    },\n175-    {\n176:      \"title\": \"Current prototype scene-builder exclusive-write lock\",\n177-      \"requirement_type\": \"pipeline_constraint\",\n178-      \"status\": \"confirmed\",\n179-      \"gdd_evidence\": [\n180-        {\n181-          \"reference\": \"Section 4 - Shared Context and Coordination Rules\",\n182:          \"requirement\": \"Scene-authoring work that changes objects generated or maintained through Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Editor/DoorPrototypeSceneBuilder.cs must take exclusive-write locks on both that builder and Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Scenes/DoorPrototype.unity.\"\n183-        }\n184-      ],\n185:      \"evidence\": \"Directly stated as a required durable process rule in Section 4; per-task applications are represented as matching exclusive_resources entries across domain workers whose implementation writes through the builder/scene.\"\n186-    },\n187-    {\n188-      \"title\": \"Development Agent Ownership Invariants\",\n189-      \"requirement_type\": \"pipeline_constraint\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
